<p class="lead">If your plumbing, HVAC, roofing, or electrical business website is stuck in 2018 — slow, clunky, and bleeding mobile leads — this is the only guide you need. We have redesigned 200+ contractor websites and distilled every critical step into a 40-point checklist. Follow it, and you will avoid the $15,000+ mistakes we see home service businesses make every month.</p>

<h2>Why Most Contractor Website Redesigns Fail (And How This Checklist Fixes That)</h2>

<p>Here is a number that should keep you up at night: <strong>38% of visitors stop engaging with a website if the layout is unattractive</strong>, according to Adobe's State of Content report. For home service contractors, that is not just a lost visitor — that is a $3,000 HVAC install or a $12,000 roof replacement walking out the digital door.</p>

<p>We have audited hundreds of contractor websites at OnwardCraft. The pattern is always the same. A business owner hires a generalist web designer who has never worked with a service company. The designer builds something pretty but functionally broken. No local SEO foundation. No conversion path. No mobile optimization. The site launches, traffic drops, and the owner assumes "websites just don't work for my industry."</p>

<p>That assumption costs contractors millions in lost revenue annually. The problem is not that websites don't work for home services. The problem is that most website redesign steps skip the parts that actually drive calls and form submissions.</p>

<h3>The Real Cost of a Bad Redesign</h3>

<p>A poorly executed contractor website redesign checklist costs you in three ways:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Direct costs:</strong> $5,000–$25,000 spent on design and development that produces zero ROI</li>
<li><strong>Opportunity costs:</strong> 6–12 months of lost leads while you fix what should have been done right the first time</li>
<li><strong>SEO damage:</strong> Rankings tank when URLs change without proper redirects, costing you organic traffic you spent years building</li>
</ul>

<p>One HVAC client came to us after a redesign dropped their organic traffic 64% in 90 days. Their previous agency changed every URL, removed location pages, and built the new site on a slow page builder. It took us eight months and $18,000 in recovery work to get them back to where they started. That is why this website redesign process exists — to prevent exactly that scenario.</p>

<h3>What Makes This Checklist Different</h3>

<p>Most website redesign checklists online are written by generic marketing blogs. They tell you to "define your goals" and "choose a color scheme" without explaining what a home service business actually needs. This checklist is different because it is built from 200+ contractor redesigns across plumbing, HVAC, roofing, electrical, pest control, and landscaping.</p>

<p>Every point on this list has been battle-tested. Every recommendation comes from a real mistake we have seen cost a contractor money. And every phase is designed to move a visitor from "just browsing" to "calling for a quote" as fast as possible.</p>

